---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="DTP — AI Readiness Operating Loop"
  description="DTP helps organisations build the AI operating loop: from adoption signal and leadership decision to focused proof and adoption evidence."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="concept operating-loop">

    <!-- ─── HERO ─── -->
    <section class="ol-hero">
      <div class="ol-hero-mesh" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ma-container ol-hero-grid">

        <div class="ol-copy">
          <span class="ol-eyebrow">// operating_loop.ai_readiness</span>
          <h1>Useful AI work is a loop, not a project.</h1>
          <p class="ol-lead">Most organisations have AI activity. Very few have the loop: evidence that informs decisions, decisions that qualify builds, and builds that produce operating evidence. DTP helps you build and run it.</p>
          <div class="ol-hero-actions">
            <a class="ma-btn ma-btn-mint" href="https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/f0762b9af6a94ed2add9818a4f3ca4e5@digitaltechnologypartner.ai/meetingtype/qc2lOXjEdkO6GkMS_jZJrQ2?anonymous" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a Discovery Call</a>
            <a class="ma-btn ma-btn-outline" href="#ol-phases">See the phases →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <aside class="loop-register" aria-label="Operating loop register">
          <div class="lr-header">
            <div>
              <div class="lr-label">loop.operating_register</div>
              <div class="lr-sublabel">evidence / decision / build / adoption</div>
            </div>
            <div class="lr-cycle">cycle&ensp;∞</div>
          </div>
          <div class="lr-table">
            <div class="lr-row lr-row-done">
              <span class="lr-num">01</span>
              <span class="lr-phase">Listen</span>
              <span class="lr-output">adoption signal</span>
              <span class="lr-badge lr-badge-done">done</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lr-row lr-row-done">
              <span class="lr-num">02</span>
              <span class="lr-phase">Diagnose</span>
              <span class="lr-output">readiness evidence</span>
              <span class="lr-badge lr-badge-done">done</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lr-row lr-row-active">
              <span class="lr-num">03</span>
              <span class="lr-phase">Decide</span>
              <span class="lr-output">qualified decisions</span>
              <span class="lr-badge lr-badge-active">active</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lr-row lr-row-pending">
              <span class="lr-num">04</span>
              <span class="lr-phase">Build</span>
              <span class="lr-output">operating proof</span>
              <span class="lr-badge lr-badge-pending">pending</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lr-row lr-row-pending">
              <span class="lr-num">05</span>
              <span class="lr-phase">Adopt</span>
              <span class="lr-output">adoption evidence</span>
              <span class="lr-badge lr-badge-pending">pending</span>
            </div>
            <div class="lr-loopback" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="lr-loopback-text">↩ loops back to 01</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="lr-footer">
            <span>current decision</span>
            <strong>Narrow the highest-confidence workflow to a focused proof.</strong>
          </div>
        </aside>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── THREE OPERATIONAL TRUTHS ─── -->
    <section class="ol-band">
      <div class="ma-container ol-band-grid">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>The activity is already in motion.</h3>
          <p>Teams are using AI tools — often without shared training, governance, or any operating picture of what is actually happening.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Without a loop, the evidence disappears.</h3>
          <p>Each pilot, demo and experiment produces signal. Without a loop to capture and use it, leadership keeps making decisions from scratch.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>The loop makes the next decision easier.</h3>
          <p>When evidence from each phase feeds the next, build commitments become narrower, faster to justify, and more likely to deliver.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── FIVE LOOP PHASES ─── -->
    <section class="ol-phases" id="ol-phases">
      <div class="ma-container">
        <div class="ol-phases-intro">
          <span class="ma-section-tag">// loop.phase_sequence</span>
          <h2>Five phases. Each one produces evidence the next depends on.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="ol-phase-list">
          <div class="ol-phase-item">
            <div class="ol-phase-left">
              <span class="ol-phase-num">01</span>
              <h3>Listen</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="ol-phase-right">
              <p>Capture where AI is already touching work, where pressure is building, and which processes have the conditions for change.</p>
              <div class="ol-phase-output">
                <span class="opo-label">produces</span>
                <span class="opo-value">Adoption signal</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-phase-item">
            <div class="ol-phase-left">
              <span class="ol-phase-num">02</span>
              <h3>Diagnose</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="ol-phase-right">
              <p>Separate enthusiasm from evidence. Score readiness across value potential, data quality, governance, capability and adoption appetite.</p>
              <div class="ol-phase-output">
                <span class="opo-label">produces</span>
                <span class="opo-value">Readiness evidence</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-phase-item">
            <div class="ol-phase-left">
              <span class="ol-phase-num">03</span>
              <h3>Decide</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="ol-phase-right">
              <p>Give leadership a concrete choice for each opportunity: encourage, control, investigate, stop or prove. Not a recommendation — a decision.</p>
              <div class="ol-phase-output">
                <span class="opo-label">produces</span>
                <span class="opo-value">Qualified decisions</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-phase-item">
            <div class="ol-phase-left">
              <span class="ol-phase-num">04</span>
              <h3>Build</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="ol-phase-right">
              <p>Where evidence supports it, deliver the narrow proof — PoC, MVP, internal tool or workflow agent. Only where readiness is real.</p>
              <div class="ol-phase-output">
                <span class="opo-label">produces</span>
                <span class="opo-value">Operating proof</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-phase-item ol-phase-last">
            <div class="ol-phase-left">
              <span class="ol-phase-num">05</span>
              <h3>Adopt</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="ol-phase-right">
              <p>Track whether the work changes the process, improves decisions, and earns continued investment. This data feeds the next Listen phase.</p>
              <div class="ol-phase-output">
                <span class="opo-label">produces</span>
                <span class="opo-value opo-value-loop">Adoption evidence ↩ 01</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── WHAT THE LOOP MAKES POSSIBLE ─── -->
    <section class="ol-outcomes">
      <div class="ma-container">
        <div class="ol-outcomes-intro">
          <span class="ol-tag-dark">// loop.when_it_runs</span>
          <h2>What a working loop makes possible.</h2>
          <p>The organisations getting reliable AI value are not running better demos. They are running a loop that keeps the operating evidence visible and the decisions well-qualified.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ol-outcome-grid">
          <div class="ol-outcome-card">
            <b>Visibility</b>
            <p>Leadership knows where AI is touching work — before the next budget conversation or risk audit.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-outcome-card">
            <b>Qualified decisions</b>
            <p>The organisation stops treating every AI idea as equal. Some get encouraged. Some get controlled. A few get proved.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-outcome-card">
            <b>Faster proofs</b>
            <p>When evidence exists, the build gets narrower. Success criteria get clearer. The commitment gets easier to justify.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-outcome-card">
            <b>Compounding evidence</b>
            <p>Adoption data from each proof feeds back into the next Listen phase. Each cycle starts with better signal than the last.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── SERVICES ─── -->
    <section class="ol-services">
      <div class="ma-container">
        <div class="ol-services-intro">
          <span class="ma-section-tag">// dtp.service_stack</span>
          <h2>Four services that support the loop.</h2>
          <p>Each can stand alone. Together they give the loop a route from first signal to operating proof.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ol-svc-cols">
          <div class="ol-svc-col">
            <div class="ol-svc-top"><div class="ol-svc-node"></div></div>
            <div class="ol-svc-body">
              <div class="ol-svc-meta">
                <span class="osm-num">01</span>
                <span class="osm-phase">Entry point</span>
              </div>
              <h3>AI Readiness Snapshot</h3>
              <p>A low-friction signal for leaders who need to know whether there is enough substance to go deeper.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-svc-col">
            <div class="ol-svc-top"><div class="ol-svc-node"></div></div>
            <div class="ol-svc-body">
              <div class="ol-svc-meta">
                <span class="osm-num">02</span>
                <span class="osm-phase">Evidence base</span>
              </div>
              <h3>AI Readiness Diagnostic</h3>
              <p>A structured look at adoption, appetite, risk, process opportunity, data and capability across the organisation.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-svc-col">
            <div class="ol-svc-top"><div class="ol-svc-node"></div></div>
            <div class="ol-svc-body">
              <div class="ol-svc-meta">
                <span class="osm-num">03</span>
                <span class="osm-phase">Leadership layer</span>
              </div>
              <h3>AI Readiness Advisory</h3>
              <p>Interpretation and challenge so leadership can make the next decision rather than admire the data.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ol-svc-col ol-svc-col-final">
            <div class="ol-svc-top"><div class="ol-svc-node ol-svc-node-final"></div></div>
            <div class="ol-svc-body">
              <div class="ol-svc-meta">
                <span class="osm-num">04</span>
                <span class="osm-phase">Committed build</span>
              </div>
              <h3>Focused AI Builds</h3>
              <p>Focused builds where the diagnostic shows a worthwhile use case and an owner who can absorb and use the result.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ─── CTA ─── -->
    <section class="ol-cta">
      <div class="ma-container ol-cta-inner">
        <h2>Build the loop before you build the next AI thing.</h2>
        <p>When you know where the evidence sits, the next decision is easier to make and easier to justify.</p>
        <a class="ma-btn ma-btn-mint ma-btn-lg" href="https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/f0762b9af6a94ed2add9818a4f3ca4e5@digitaltechnologypartner.ai/meetingtype/qc2lOXjEdkO6GkMS_jZJrQ2?anonymous" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a Discovery Call</a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* ─── LOCAL UTILITIES ─── */
  .ol-hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .ol-cta {
    background: var(--ma-bg);
    padding: 7rem 0 8rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ma-border);
  }
  .ol-cta-inner {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .ol-cta-inner h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .ol-cta-inner p { color: rgba(255,255,255,.72); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .ol-cta-inner .ma-btn { margin-top: 2.25rem; }

  /* ─── BASE ─── */
  .operating-loop { background: var(--ma-bg); }

  /* ─── HERO ─── */
  .ol-hero {
    padding: 10rem 0 5.5rem;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ol-hero-mesh {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 60% at 74% 36%, rgba(0,229,160,.065) 0%, transparent 65%),
      radial-gradient(ellipse 45% 55% at 14% 74%, rgba(30,50,180,.05) 0%, transparent 60%);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .ol-hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr .95fr;
    gap: 4.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .ol-eyebrow {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .72rem;
    color: var(--ma-mint);
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
  }

  .ol-copy h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 7vw, 6.4rem);
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.06em;
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .ol-lead {
    font-size: 1.16rem;
    max-width: 580px;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.78);
    margin: 1.4rem 0 2.2rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* ─── LOOP REGISTER ─── */
  .loop-register {
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, #15152a 0%, #0e0e1e 100%);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);
    border-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow:
      0 32px 100px rgba(0,0,0,.52),
      inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(0,229,160,.04);
  }

  .lr-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem .9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.025);
  }

  .lr-label {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .76rem;
    color: var(--ma-white);
    letter-spacing: .03em;
  }

  .lr-sublabel {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .62rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.52);
    margin-top: .22rem;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
  }

  .lr-cycle {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .68rem;
    color: var(--ma-mint);
    background: rgba(0,229,160,.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,229,160,.2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: .25rem .55rem;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  /* Register rows */
  .lr-table { padding: .35rem 0; }

  .lr-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.4rem 6.5rem 1fr 5.6rem;
    align-items: center;
    gap: .5rem;
    padding: .72rem 1.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.04);
  }
  .lr-row:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }

  .lr-num {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: .05em;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.48);
  }

  .lr-phase {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-display);
    font-size: .92rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.68);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .lr-output {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .67rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.54);
    letter-spacing: .02em;
  }

  .lr-badge {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .56rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    padding: .2rem .44rem;
    border-radius: 3px;
    text-align: center;
    justify-self: end;
  }

  /* Done rows — muted */
  .lr-row-done { opacity: .72; }
  .lr-badge-done {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.58);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16);
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.04);
  }

  /* Active row — mint highlight */
  .lr-row-active { background: rgba(0,229,160,.055); }
  .lr-row-active .lr-num { color: var(--ma-mint); }
  .lr-row-active .lr-phase { color: var(--ma-white); }
  .lr-row-active .lr-output { color: rgba(0,229,160,.68); }
  .lr-badge-active {
    color: var(--ma-mint);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,229,160,.3);
    background: rgba(0,229,160,.1);
  }

  /* Pending rows — dim */
  .lr-badge-pending {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.48);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);
    background: transparent;
  }

  /* Loop-back indicator */
  .lr-loopback {
    padding: .52rem 1.4rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed rgba(0,229,160,.14);
    margin-top: .25rem;
  }
  .lr-loopback-text {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .6rem;
    color: rgba(0,229,160,.68);
    letter-spacing: .04em;
  }

  .lr-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: .9rem 1.4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.07);
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.02);
  }
  .lr-footer span {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .6rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.5);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .07em;
    white-space: nowrap;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .lr-footer strong {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-display);
    font-size: .95rem;
    color: var(--ma-white);
    line-height: 1.32;
  }

  /* ─── THREE TRUTHS BAND ─── */
  .ol-band {
    background: #0c0c14;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    padding: 5rem 0;
  }

  .ol-band-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .ol-band-grid article {
    background: #0c0c14;
    padding: 2.4rem 2.1rem;
    min-height: 240px;
    transition: background .2s;
  }
  .ol-band-grid article:hover { background: #0f0f1c; }

  .ol-band-grid span {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    color: var(--ma-mint);
    font-size: .76rem;
  }

  .ol-band-grid h3 {
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 .75rem;
    color: var(--ma-white);
    line-height: 1.18;
  }

  .ol-band-grid p {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.66);
    line-height: 1.68;
    font-size: .97rem;
  }

  /* ─── FIVE LOOP PHASES ─── */
  .ol-phases {
    background: #0f0f1d;
    padding: 7rem 0 6rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
  }

  .ol-phases-intro {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .ol-phases-intro h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.8rem);
    line-height: 1.04;
    letter-spacing: -.04em;
    margin: .6rem 0 0;
  }

  .ol-phase-list { border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1); }

  .ol-phase-item {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 3.5rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.06);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .ol-phase-last { border-bottom: none; }

  .ol-phase-left {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: .4rem;
    padding-top: .15rem;
  }

  .ol-phase-num {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .76rem;
    color: var(--ma-mint);
    letter-spacing: .06em;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .ol-phase-left h3 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -.04em;
    color: var(--ma-white);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ol-phase-right p {
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.76);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.72;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
    max-width: 540px;
  }

  .ol-phase-output {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: .55rem;
  }

  .opo-label {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .6rem;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.32);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .07em;
  }

  .opo-value {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .72rem;
    color: var(--ma-mint);
    letter-spacing: .03em;
    background: rgba(0,229,160,.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,229,160,.2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: .2rem .52rem;
  }

  .opo-value-loop {
    background: rgba(0,229,160,.12);
    border-color: rgba(0,229,160,.28);
  }

  /* ─── OUTCOMES — light editorial section ─── */
  .ol-outcomes {
    background: #edeae0;
    color: #0f101a;
    padding: 7rem 0 6.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(15,16,26,.08);
  }

  .ol-outcomes-intro {
    max-width: 580px;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .ol-tag-dark {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--ma-font-mono);
    font-size: .7rem;
    letter-spacing: .09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6a7080;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .ol-outcomes-intro h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.2vw, 3.8rem);
    line-height: 1.03;
    letter-spacing: -.04em;
    color: #0f101a;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .ol-outcomes-intro p {
    color: #42485a;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ol-outcome-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .ol-outcome-card {
    background: #f4f1e8;
    border: 1px solid rgba(15,16,26,.1);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1.8rem;
    transition: border-color .18s;
  }
  .ol-outcome-card:hover { border-color: rgba(0,160,110,.28); }

  .ol-outcome-card b {
    font-family: var(--ma-font-display);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: #0f101a;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: .55rem;
  }

  .ol-outcome-card p {
